mfd: macsmc: initialise the atomic-write spinlock

smc->lock (used by apple_smc_write_atomic(), i.e. macsmc-reboot) was never
spin_lock_init()ed; it only worked because the struct is zero-allocated and
CONFIG_DEBUG_SPINLOCK is off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
index 31540f67d..68f7bb832 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
@@ -419,6 +419,7 @@ static int apple_smc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	mutex_init(&smc->mutex);
+	spin_lock_init(&smc->lock);
 	smc->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	smc->sram_base = devm_platform_get_and_ioremap_resource(pdev, 1, &smc->sram);
 	if (IS_ERR(smc->sram_base))
